{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 135 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "c39e5c6ff1e1774323273dcad9740c3c6805546e21659b8dc7a171cd867291fe" :edb/db-before-t 134 :edb/db-after-t 135 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533447 50 #inst "2026-10-10T22:36:56.855Z" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186059742 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365561 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186059742 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366197 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186059743 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366204 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186059853 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364954 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186059854 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366800 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186059855 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365553 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186059855 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365556 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186060026 1068 #edb/ref 17592186056484 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186060026 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364961 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186060026 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186060026 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $M$ given below?\n\n- $det(M)=10$\n- $det(M)=-5$\n- $M$ is a singular matrix\n\n \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186060026 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $M$ given below?\n\n1. $det(M) = 10$\n2. $det(M) =-5$\n3. $M$ is a singular matrix\n\n$M = \\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186060026 1074 "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 4\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{1}{3}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}(12-15)-0+\\frac{1}{3}(0+9\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\cdot (-3)+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{5}+3\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(M)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186064258 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365459 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186064259 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365896 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186064260 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366280 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186068695 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364865 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186068696 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365803 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186068697 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365574 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186069238 1068 #edb/ref 17592186066576 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186069238 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365568 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186069238 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186069238 1071 "${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{({x}^{2}-1)^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}}=$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186069238 1071 "What is $lim_(x → 0)((x^{2} - 1)^{2} - 1)/(x^{2})$?" 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186069238 1074 "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{({x}^{2}-1)^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[({x}^{2}-1)^{2}-1]}^{′}}{{[{x}^{2}]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{4x({x}^{2}-1)}{2x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{4{x}^{3}-4x}{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{({x}^{2}-1)^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{4{x}^{3}-4x}{2x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[4{x}^{3}-4x]^{′}}{[2x]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{12{x}^{2}-4}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12(0)^{2}-4}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083086 1071 "What is the center of the hyperbola \n![](images/57/57e159560b79e8383e6a2eec7a8f8dd6568fbf0fb8dae9f5277d35a166b6402a.png)" 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186083086 1071 "What is the center of the hyperbola \n![](images/5e/5e01d30ade2c26c6befcc21339aff858a2cfaaec406df7428cc9770d70903ce2.png)" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083086 1074 "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at ![](images/2a/2ac743df1895cd3a2185fadc273945035e01ff93c9bda9394f6b37eeaeba7e7d.png) is given by\n![](images/81/813e411586523b884a123a4794c1cb06d7b95f675ca75e1b994c6b09c3fe6a92.png)\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group ![](images/d1/d158d97a9b8654a3178eaed05119d604b49295b63e914dc468153bfd7cea88bc.png) and ![](images/67/6752ce15229c41002c859a3e31d785189a80c096d49c3b85ab011d3ce9506d1c.png) terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n![](images/f5/f5e8733c3f7e629ea43c6e37f69f796f8fa66a88e10e978eb944a8ebc01e0009.png)\n\nTherefore, the center is ![](images/1c/1cbb0b8cf874096a80504a2f37e87f6b7ced32f3129a9e7e4ab0348753e91bfe.png)" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083086 1074 "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at ![](images/6c/6c305528045f15b88bbb08bcbb70e321036d4c901b971d2d9f37ec0fc14c5bab.png) is given by\n![](images/42/42df0f3278c4cf754f5e3c65787c2640a0c084ab1e79874dd3c071a97012b0dd.png)\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group ![](images/6c/6c64f050494f28920cf5518293243a78d46e5fa2758fc8f470fdb466586effbc.png) and ![](images/75/751725803c8443e8ccea32f24624965f57b739dab31251b837c5a86ecee96f43.png) terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n![](images/fc/fc13c27b687a2bfbf369fc03321ee89736bd1b2383871bf8ceac7457e2c35591.png)\n\nTherefore, the center is ![](images/dd/dd3932b5cb055c4ae37e61384441deddc8626e4257ceb60b596325981b64710d.png)" 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186083212 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365595 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083212 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366343 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083303 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366322 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083303 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366329 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083304 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365585 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083304 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365590 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083305 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364879 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083305 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365600 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083305 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366336 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083569 1068 #edb/ref 17592186080279 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186083569 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365384 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083569 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083569 1071 "What is the center of the hyperbola\n$-2x^{2} + 5y^{2} + 12x - 60y =-152$?" 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186083569 1071 "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$-2{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}+12x-60y=-152?$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186083569 1074 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}+12x-60y & =-152 \\\\ 5{y}^{2}-60y-2{x}^{2}+12x & =-152 \\\\ 5[{y}^{2}-12y]-2[{x}^{2}-6x] & =-152 \\\\ 5[(y-6)^{2}-36]-2[(x-3)^{2}-9] & =-152 \\\\ 5(y-6)^{2}-180-2(x-3)^{2}+18 & =-152 \\\\ 5(y-6)^{2}-2(x-3)^{2} & =-152+180-18 \\\\ 5(y-6)^{2}-2(x-3)^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(y-6)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{5} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(3,6).$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186092280 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366405 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186096638 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366164 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186096639 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365577 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186096658 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365580 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186096707 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364886 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186096838 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364872 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186097052 1068 #edb/ref 17592186094255 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186097052 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364900 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186097052 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186097052 1071 "![](images/c2/c2406e6f3cb76f50bfcc73a348b38d93b7a24da8e4314e0b3523bb4cbf143364.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $OA^(→) = a$, $OB^(→) = b$, and $T$ divides $AB^(―)$ in the ratio $AT: TB = 1: 1$. Find $OT^(→)$." 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186097052 1071 "![](images/c2/c2406e6f3cb76f50bfcc73a348b38d93b7a24da8e4314e0b3523bb4cbf143364.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OB}=b$, and $T$ divides $\\overset{―}{AB}$ in the ratio $AT:TB=1:1.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OT}.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186097052 1074 "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=a,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{AT}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OAB,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-a+b \\\\  & =b-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $AT:TB=1:1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AT}=\\frac{1}{2}\\overset{\\to }{AB}=\\frac{1}{2}(b-a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OT} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT} \\\\  & =a+\\frac{1}{2}(b-a) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}a+\\frac{1}{2}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186097268 1068 #edb/ref 17592186095502 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186097268 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366158 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186097268 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186097268 1071 "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b$, given that $\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^{b}f(x)dx = lim_(n → ∞)∑_(k = 0)^(n - 1)[(2 + \\frac{5k}{n})^{2} \\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]$." 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186097268 1071 "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that ${\\int }_{2}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{(2+\\frac{5k}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}].$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186097268 1074 "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=2.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{5}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{n}=\\frac{b-2}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=7.\n$$\n\nConsequently, ${x}_{k}=2+\\frac{5k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})={x}_{k}^{2}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{7}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{(2+\\frac{5k}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(x)={x}^{2}$ and $b=7.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186115066 1071 "Consider the matrix\n![](images/a5/a58c9caa0812b56d74f38a457c3f39e72a3fd365a881d4128cfd55c1773e05f6.png)\nFind $f(D)$ if $f(X)=-X^2+3X+2.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186115066 1071 "Consider the matrix\n![](images/b0/b070684b11de0098cac091b9132ef6276679177fa6dce1a8129f7951f6013c8c.png)\nFind $f(D)$ if $f(X)=-X^2+3X+2.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186115235 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365504 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186115235 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365513 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186115235 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365524 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186115236 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365535 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186115236 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365544 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186115236 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366308 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186115236 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366315 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186115360 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365184 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186119743 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364940 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186119744 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365730 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186119745 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364947 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186119846 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365889 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186119846 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366357 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186119887 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364673 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186119941 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364967 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186119942 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366211 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186120275 1068 #edb/ref 17592186117759 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186120275 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365792 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186120275 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186120275 1071 "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t) = ⟨t + 1, 8\\ln t, 2t^{2} + 3⟩$ at the point $P(2, 0, 5)$?" 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186120275 1071 "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨t+1,\\,8\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2{t}^{2}+3⟩$ at the point $P(2,0,5)?$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186120275 1074 "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(2,0,5)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨2,0,5⟩ \\\\ ⟨t+1,\\,8\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2{t}^{2}+3⟩ & =⟨2,0,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}t+1=2 \\\\ 8\\operatorname{ln}⁡t=0 \\\\ 2{t}^{2}+3=5.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=1.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(2,0,5)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}+3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,\\frac{8}{t},\\,4t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =⟨1,\\,\\frac{8}{1},\\,4(1)⟩=⟨1,8,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{8}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+64+16} \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(2,0,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}⟨1,8,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\frac{8}{9},\\frac{4}{9}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186124511 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366239 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186124523 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364974 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592