l that the hyperbola\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{z^2}{4} - \\dfrac{x^2}{16} = 1\n$$\n\nfor\n\n$$\nz \\geq 2\n$$\n\nin $xz$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n\\langle x, z \\rangle = \\big \\langle 4\\tan{t}, \\, 2\\sec{t} \\big\\rangle, \\qquad t \\in \\left(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n$$\n\nsince\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{z^{2}}{4} - \\frac{x^{2}}{16} &= ((2\\sec t)^{2})/(4) - ((4\\tan t)^{2})/(16) \\\\\n&= \\frac{4\\sec^{2} t}{4} - \\frac{16\\tan^{2} t}{16} \\\\\n&= \\sec^{2} t - \\tan^{2} t \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(t, y) &= ⟨x, y, z⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨4\\tan t, y, 2\\sec t⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nt \\in \\left(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}, \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n$$\n\nand $y \\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$.\n\nTherefore, the third component of $\\mathbf{f}$ is ${\\color{blue}2\\sec{t}}$." 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186175829 1074 "Recall that the hyperbola $\\dfrac{z^2}{4} - \\dfrac{x^2}{16} = 1$ for $z \\geq 2$ in $xz$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n\\langle x , z \\rangle = \\big \\langle 4\\tan{t}, \\, 2\\sec{t} \\big\\rangle,\n\n\\qquad t \\in \\left(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{(2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)^{2}}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{sec}^{2}⁡t}{4}-\\frac{16{tan}^{2}⁡t}{16} \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡t-{tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,y) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y,\\,2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in \\left(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}, \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$ and $y \\in (-\\infty, \\infty).$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $\\mathbf{f}$ is ${\\color{blue}2\\sec{t}}.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175861 1071 "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nLet $Y=2-4X.$ Calculate $P(Y \\gt 2).$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175861 1071 "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nLet $Y=2-4X$. Calculate $P(Y \\gt 2)$." 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186175861 1074 "First, let's add a $Y = 2-4X$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nNow, $f_X(x) = f_Y(y)$ for corresponding values of $X$ and $Y.$ So, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y>2) & =P(Y=3)+P(Y=4) \\\\  & =0.2+0.25 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175861 1074 "First, let's add a $Y = 2-4X$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nNow,\n\n$$\nf_X(x) = f_Y(y)\n$$\n\nfor corresponding values of $X$ and $Y$. So, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(Y > 2) &= P(Y = 3) + P(Y = 4) \\\\\n&= 0.2 + 0.25 \\\\\n&= 0.45\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186175862 1071 "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nLet $Y=2-4X.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $a$ | $3$ | $c$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.25$ | $b$ | $0.1$ | $d$ | $0.3$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175862 1071 "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nLet $Y=2-4X$. The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $a$ | $3$ | $c$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.25$ | $b$ | $0.1$ | $d$ | $0.3$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c$?" 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186175862 1074 "First, let's add a $Y = 2-4X$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nNow, $f_X(x) = f_Y(y)$ for corresponding values of $X$ and $Y.$ Therefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nSo, we have $a=4, b=0.2, c=2,$ and therefore $a+b+c =6.2.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175862 1074 "First, let's add a $Y = 2-4X$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nNow,\n\n$$\nf_X(x) = f_Y(y)\n$$\n\nfor corresponding values of $X$ and $Y$. Therefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\na=4, b=0.2, c=2\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\na+b+c =6.2\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 false] [17592186175931 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365972 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175931 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365977 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175931 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365982 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175931 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365985 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175932 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364893 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175932 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365990 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175932 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365995 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175932 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366412 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175932 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366419 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175961 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366000 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175961 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366003 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175961 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366232 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175961 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366468 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175961 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366475 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175970 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364680 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175976 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365432 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175976 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365439 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175976 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365446 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175978 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365404 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175978 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365411 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175979 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365418 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175979 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365425 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186175983 1038 #edb/