7592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364850 1084 #uuid "b9118962-8fff-5461-a4b1-95a1ae553944" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364851 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364852 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364851 1069 "q-111774" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364851 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364851 1071 "Consider the standard matrices of three linear transformations shown below. Which of the transformations map ${R}^{2}$ onto $(0,0)?$\n\n$$\n{T}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{T}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{T}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364851 1072 #uuid "47539370-0241-5c5a-be9d-00783bbc307e" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364851 1074 "Given a linear transformation over ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ we have the following:\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto ${R}^{2}$ if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=2,$ i.e., $T$ is nonsingular.\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=1.$\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto $(0,0)$ if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=0,$ i.e., $T$ is the zero matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- ${T}_{1}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto $(0,0)$ since ${T}_{1}$ is the zero matrix, i.e. $\\text{rank}({T}_{1})=0.$\n\n- ${T}_{2}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto ${R}^{2}.$ Indeed, ${T}_{2}$ is a nonsingular matrix, i.e. $\\text{rank}({T}_{2})=2.$\n\n- ${T}_{3}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line. Notice that the columns of ${T}_{3}$ are linearly dependent but it's not the zero matrix. So, $\\text{rank}({T}_{3})=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ only.\"" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364852 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364853 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364852 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364854 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364852 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364855 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364852 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364856 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364852 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364857 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364852 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364852 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364852 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364855 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364852 1080 #uuid "03d7334c-0ff0-5553-b1c2-886da95f9dc0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364853 1081 "${T}_{2}$ only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364853 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364853 1084 #uuid "709c3c3c-624d-59ae-844b-5e91f0bcb6bd" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364854 1081 "${T}_{1}$, ${T}_{2}$, and ${T}_{3}$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364854 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364854 1084 #uuid "270d29d1-c33c-5b5b-9833-a4772f59100b" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364855 1081 "${T}_{1}$ only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364855 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364855 1084 #uuid "b0f8a93e-70fd-5d0e-9eab-8677a1c620ff" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364856 1081 "${T}_{3}$ only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364856 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364856 1084 #uuid "ddc5620c-fba6-5c6e-aab3-b60ca4539af0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364857 1081 "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364857 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364857 1084 #uuid "828b5c4b-a420-5f01-bee8-d7e332049730" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364858 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364859 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364858 1069 "q-113501" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364858 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364858 1071 "The domain of the function $f(x)=\\frac{4x+3}{5x+2k}$ is $(-\\infty ,\\frac{2}{5})\\cup (\\frac{2}{5},\\infty ).$ What is the value of $k?$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364858 1072 #uuid "ee16459a-bf12-529f-aa3b-cc89f5e9cb99" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364858 1074 "A reciprocal function is defined for all values of $x$ except for those that make the denominator zero. So, to find the domain, we must exclude all values that make the denominator zero.\n\nSetting the denominator equal to zero and solving, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2k & =0 \\\\ 5x & =-2k \\\\ x & =-\\frac{2k}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the point that must be excluded from the domain is $x=-\\frac{2k}{5}.$ \n\nOn the other hand, we can see that $x=\\frac{2}{5}$ is excluded from the domain. Equating this to $-\\frac{2k}{5},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2k}{5} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{k}{5} & =-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364859 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364860 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364859 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364861 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364859 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364862 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364859 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364863 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364859 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364864 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364859 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364859 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364859 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364864 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364859 1080 #uuid "6c3b44ec-e362-5848-b757-e1a30a3bc178" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364860 1081 "-5" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364860 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364860 1084 #uuid "a2016816-28e8-5d51-9785-1496f42addb7" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364861 1081 "3" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364861 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364861 1084 #uuid "a1103bae-8319-57e0-97ad-c5f4b71339b0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364862 1081 "2" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364862 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364862 1084 #uuid "58d4f932-503e-5417-a6ef-0f99b77003fd" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364863 1081 "1" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364863 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364863 1084 #uuid "7872df49-3602-579a-81a7-9757623ee8c0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364864 1081 "-1" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364864 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364864 1084 #uuid "51e49929-146d-5950-b7fb-a559e7e56524" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364865 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364866 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364865 1069 "q-114240" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364865 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364865 1071 "${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{x}-x-1}=$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364865 1072 #uuid "52b4d998-08c9-5b8e-9e74-1ff6d7cb2d7c" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364865 1074 "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{x}-x-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[{x}^{2}]^{′}}{[{e}^{x}-x-1]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2x}{{e}^{x}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x-1+{e}^{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2x}{{e}^{x}-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[2x]^{′}}{[{e}^{x}-1]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364866 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364867 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364866 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364868 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364866 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364869 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364866 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364870 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364866 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364871 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364866 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364866 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364866 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364868 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364866 1080 #uuid "69e5b2f1-392f-5128-8f9c-fc9d2c8d33cc" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364867 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364867 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364867 1084 #uuid "49851532-30c7-5fc0-9a39-59ad1c1338ba" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364868 1081 "2" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364868 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364868 1084 #uuid "839ff078-d526-5536-a690-24a2142f02a5" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364869 1081 "1" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364869 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364869 1084 #uuid "76a5277b-e0ab-5edc-8236-c78fdd77539b" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364870 1081 "-1" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364870 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186364870 1084 #uuid "f97e7d20-8b29-5dc1-bb6d-71fa6f9401