 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365010 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365011 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365010 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365012 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365010 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365013 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365010 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365014 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365010 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365015 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365010 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365010 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365010 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365011 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365010 1080 #uuid "0051ff91-5982-5f79-8021-15f6e5a79345" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365011 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365011 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365011 1084 #uuid "1c8cc9b5-4fea-51be-8530-093f28bb182d" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365012 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365012 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365012 1084 #uuid "d8437765-1667-5b4a-a2d4-519d741042f9" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365013 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365013 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365013 1084 #uuid "80156ccd-7acc-5a08-958d-43e718870bf6" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365014 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365014 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365014 1084 #uuid "46e97d17-2170-52e4-bae8-f1a4b26c06f1" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365015 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365015 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365015 1084 #uuid "bb6446d2-ce20-5814-95a8-6fcf987d8011" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365016 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365017 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365016 1069 "q-140554" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365016 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365016 1071 "Which of the following equations define a non-empty set of points in the ${x}_{1}{x}_{2}$-plane?\n\n- ${x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}=-1$\n- ${x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}=0$\n- ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=0$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365016 1072 #uuid "d7ec5e81-6115-5881-b6f7-16bb9226da5a" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365016 1074 "Let's examine each of the equations in turn.\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}=-1$ defines a non-empty set. It represents the hyperbola ${x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2}=1.$\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}=0$ defines a non-empty set. It represents a parabola that opens in the direction of the negative ${x}_{2}$-axis in the ${x}_{1}{x}_{2}$-plane.\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=0$ defines a non-empty set. It represents a single point $(0,0)$ in the ${x}_{1}{x}_{2}$-plane.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365017 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365018 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365017 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365019 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365017 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365020 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365017 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365021 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365017 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365022 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365017 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365017 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365017 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365018 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365017 1080 #uuid "713649dd-841d-595d-ad2c-1d706d7c2e1a" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365018 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365018 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365018 1084 #uuid "ebbc61b3-da42-52b4-8b9a-1c8bfc6e51d4" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365019 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365019 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365019 1084 #uuid "e57b11cb-0a00-5658-98f3-d87f6a7775f5" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365020 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365020 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365020 1084 #uuid "259d1b4b-cb8c-5458-acca-8cb674f94596" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365021 1081 "III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365021 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365021 1084 #uuid "e7d2ca84-53fb-576d-85e4-ed21ca559e67" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365022 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365022 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365022 1084 #uuid "088b9f24-a8df-521a-bfbe-dbaa748a06e6" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365023 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365024 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365023 1069 "q-140557" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365023 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365023 1071 "What type of quadratic curve is defined by the following equation?\n\n$$\n4{x}_{1}^{2}+16{x}_{1}=-7\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365023 1072 #uuid "59ff20d8-dfd7-5f57-8dd7-676de1c62793" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365023 1074 "First, we complete the squares for the variable ${x}_{1}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}^{2}+16{x}_{1} & =-7 \\\\ 4({x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}+4-4) & =-7 \\\\ 4({x}_{1}+2)^{2}-16 & =-7 \\\\ 4({x}_{1}+2)^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, performing the change of variable\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}={x}_{1}+2,\n$$\n\nwe get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}_{1}^{2} & =9 \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2} & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents the pair of parallel lines ${y}_{1}=\\frac{3}{2}$ and ${y}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365024 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365025 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365024 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365026 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365024 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365027 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365024 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365028 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365024 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365029 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365024 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365024 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365024 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365028 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365024 1080 #uuid "fa02b4c6-e130-5f57-94ca-7875e4b08f0a" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365025 1081 "A pair of intersecting lines" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365025 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365025 1084 #uuid "34b2f2de-15d8-5ab1-b00e-502c92c80ede" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365026 1081 "An empty set" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365026 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365026 1084 #uuid "4a07a491-9472-50b7-8caa-2551ff3dffe7" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365027 1081 "A parabola" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365027 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365027 1084 #uuid "d3feab1f-710d-5f7d-916d-6dccaf02ac63" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365028 1081 "A pair of parallel lines" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365028 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365028 1084 #uuid "626e74b3-c07c-5db1-8452-88dfd54f5e59" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365029 1081 "A hyperbola" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365029 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365029 1084 #uuid "83cebc46-9365-5662-a211-861041f69667" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365030 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365031 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365030 1069 "q-140561" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365030 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365030 1071 "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{61}} & \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{61}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{61}} & \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{61}}\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{13} & 2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind $|\\text{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365030 1072 #uuid "46fe346a-e4ad-51c6-9905-aaf9356199fc" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365030 1074 "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm 1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\sqrt{13}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}-0\\cdot 2| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{65}\\end{aligned}\n$