92186365107 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365108 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365107 1069 "q-143030" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365107 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365107 1071 "The number of people $N$ infected by a particular virus increases with time. The rate of change of the number of infected people is proportional to the square of the number of infected people. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of people infected by the virus at time $t?$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365107 1072 #uuid "141b5a5d-ddd8-5877-bf13-99c64ae12afa" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365107 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **number of people infected** by a particular virus $N$ **increases** with time. The **rate** of change of the number of infected people is **proportional** to the **square of the number of people infected** by the virus.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *number of infected people* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *number of infected people squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}∝{N}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number of infected people *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k{N}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365108 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365109 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365108 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365110 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365108 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365111 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365108 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365112 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365108 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365113 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365108 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365108 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365108 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365113 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365108 1080 #uuid "02644996-55c0-5996-b3fc-cfdd30efd999" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365109 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-k{N}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365109 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365109 1084 #uuid "0f90381d-5e2f-5094-98f4-35628b46b4d1" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365110 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k\\sqrt{N},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365110 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365110 1084 #uuid "482fbf95-8b59-579a-90e6-50d8a87c4afe" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365111 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{N},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365111 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365111 1084 #uuid "c89b41bf-d528-52ea-9315-071885864a4b" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365112 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{N}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365112 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365112 1084 #uuid "9c587e50-36d3-57d6-916e-8900b45e04ed" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365113 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k{N}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365113 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365113 1084 #uuid "1513a057-3e2d-5151-bd82-f056466791bc" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365114 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365115 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365114 1069 "q-143683" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365114 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365114 1071 "Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- If $A$ is *any* matrix, then ${A}^{3}$ is always symmetric.\n- The sum of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric.\n- The difference of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric." 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365114 1072 #uuid "b742394a-cffb-5df9-9fbd-181d0debffeb" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365114 1074 "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, consider the matrix \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nHowever, ${A}^{3}$ is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any two symmetric matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}+{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any two symmetric matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A-B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}-{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A-B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365115 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365116 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365115 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365117 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365115 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365118 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365115 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365119 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365115 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365120 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365115 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365115 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365115 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365117 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365115 1080 #uuid "f31b5e20-d22d-52c3-81bb-59e55a57d60a" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365116 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365116 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365116 1084 #uuid "7258d24f-d528-58e3-bb8d-5b15c46a9af0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365117 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365117 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365117 1084 #uuid "a70c03f8-563d-5b83-9505-35065df751fd" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365118 1081 "I only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365118 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365118 1084 #uuid "00e0e88e-9ec6-521a-a534-f0a0b5ee0dec" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365119 1081 "III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365119 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365119 1084 #uuid "f760828f-fdf2-54a4-8c2f-128311e32754" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365120 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365120 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365120 1084 #uuid "178e4516-7515-5ab3-a8f3-7fe32775d589" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365121 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365122 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365121 1069 "q-149647" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365121 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365121 1071 "${\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({i}^{2}+{j}^{2})=$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365121 1072 #uuid "671f8375-0214-529e-a001-961fce6318c2" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365121 1074 "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({i}^{2}+{j}^{2}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}[{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({i}^{2}+{j}^{2})] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}[({i}^{2}+{1}^{2})+({i}^{2}+{2}^{2})] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(2{i}^{2}+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we sum over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(2{i}^{2}+5) & =[2(1)^{2}+5]+[2(2)^{2}+5] \\\\  & =7+13 \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365122 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365123 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365122 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365124 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365122 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365125 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365122 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365126 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365122 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365127 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365122 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365122 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365122 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365123 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365122 1080 #uuid "90cee4e0-9976-5c17-bd79-033355be91a5" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365123 1081 "20" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365123 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365123 1084 #uuid "bec402ac-cfcc-5f12-8bc1-3d6fb7bdcf1b" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365124 1081 "22" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [1759218636