94139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365190 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365190 1084 #uuid "35887ca3-a94b-506e-8020-8cda97d2a2f0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365191 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365192 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365191 1069 "q-162490" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365191 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365191 1071 "![](images/22/22058df7ac75e085e1dc352736d1abf289e80d68f340ee63687e69d18e9b23c2.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz.$ The region of integration is shown above.\n\n*Hint: Change the order of integration to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z.$*" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365191 1072 #uuid "07a226bd-3963-51a9-8f33-263f394aef39" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365191 1074 "We cannot integrate the given integral because we cannot find a simple antiderivative of the integrand. So, we change the order of integration.\n\nWe wish to find the limits of integration ${u}_{1}(x,z),$ ${u}_{2}(x,z),$ ${v}_{1}(z),$ ${v}_{2}(z),$ $a,$ and $b$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(z)}^{{v}_{2}(z)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the region of integration $R$ can be written as a type II region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi ,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\pi ,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le y}\n$$\n\nThe region $R$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/c5/c5eec166cdce2fa4be756aa144b6a802082def0374c2b6150794cb2f0f22f1a6.png)\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z$ to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z,$ we write $R$ as a type III region and its projection $D$ onto the $xz$-plane as a type II *plane* region.\n\nTo visualize this, imagine firing an arrow through the region parallel to the $y$-axis and in the direction of increasing $y,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a93024f817970869a3dcef831abc2515fe14efac5ec9dd778701d063b8351d.png)\n\nThe arrow enters the region through the left boundary and leaves through the right boundary:\n\n- The left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x,z),$ is\n\n$$\nx=y\\,⟹\\,y=x.\n$$\n\n- The right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=\\pi .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,x\\le y\\le \\pi },\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/ec/ec3bc5a58b5521286388294b97e1449bb41548004477d6d4555c9b7b917f2bd7.png)\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type II plane region in the $xz$-plane with the right curve given by $x=\\pi .$\n\n![](images/20/205c88cdd0b8a2676bc8396760095fa238ae39acd3660ed5aba2df3726161410.png)\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{x}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}[{\\int }_{x}^{\\pi }\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}[y]_{x}^{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}\\cdot (\\pi -x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-(-1-1)\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2[z]_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365193 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365194 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365195 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365196 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365197 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365192 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365192 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365192 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365197 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365192 1080 #uuid "04472cee-3f9a-56c7-9b29-8748734c70cb" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365193 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365193 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365193 1084 #uuid "44434ece-00fb-51cd-8a49-e2cfd67708d7" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365194 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365194 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365194 1084 #uuid "0fc1ea08-fb0f-5011-824b-be7b928db8cd" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365195 1081 "\\pi " 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365195 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365195 1084 #uuid "e3196088-1e84-5e59-ad8d-fd14cb623f3d" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365196 1081 "1" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365196 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365196 1084 #uuid "098ccdac-dc81-5c2f-9cf5-304766334c8d" 1319413953