16fc44a5.png)\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x$ to $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x,$ we write $R$ as a type I region and its projection $D$ onto the $xy$-plane as a type I *plane* region.\n\nTo visualize this, imagine firing an arrow through the region parallel to the $z$-axis and in the direction of increasing $z,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/38/385eed97efeb951228a44009faf76dc676f565204885c8f0df2cee0afc1657a8.png)\n\nThe arrow enters the region through the bottom boundary and leaves through the top boundary:\n\n- The top boundary of the region, written in the form $z=z(x,y),$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{z}\\,⟺\\,z={y}^{2}.\n$$\n\n- The bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nz=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le {y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/83/837b43fa43b6d160d0734a629f08bb415bd91f382b99dbd6a5c227dd46b98f29.png)\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I plane region in the $xy$-plane with the top curve given by $y=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n![](images/90/90dc40b39cd7a3fdfcff0469b1915dcd64811a16aad0dad452c8f57d4118546b.png)\n\nHence, we have that\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration so that it is integrated first with respect to $z,$ then $y,$ then $x,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{z}}^{3}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365199 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365200 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365199 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365201 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365199 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365202 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365199 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365203 13194139533447 17592186045585 t