ned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}x(1+2\\lambda )=0 \\\\ y(\\lambda +3)=\\lambda \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we break it up into several cases:\n\n- Assuming $x=0$ in the first equation of the system, the constraint condition $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2y=0$ implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-2y & =0\\,⇒\\,y=0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical points $(0,0),(0,2).$\n\n- Assuming $\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}$ in the first equation of the system, the second equation of the system implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-\\frac{1}{2}+3)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,⇒\\,y=-\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the constraint condition $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2y=0$ implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}=-\\frac{11}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a contradiction.\n\nTherefore, $f$ has possible extreme values at the points\n\n$$\n(0,0),\\,(0,2).\n$$\n\nWe evaluate $f$ at these points. These are given in the following table:\n\n| $(x,y)$ | $(0,0)$ | $(0,2)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x,y)$ | $1$ | $-11$ |\n\nTherefore, the function reaches a maximum value at the point $(0,0)$ and its maximum value is $1.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365221 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365222 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365223 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365224 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365220 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365225 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365220 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365220 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365220 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365224 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365220 1080 #uuid "30f4541b-0d8a-526a-afe2-a9aa2ea8fd81" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365221 1081 "9" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365221 1083 #edb/ref 175