e $(10+kx)\\,{m/s}^{2}$ and is directed *toward* $O,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-(10+kx).\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}),\n$$\n\nwe can rewrite our equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})=-(10+kx).\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides of the above equation with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})\\text{d}x=\\int -(10+kx)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwhich gives the general solution\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}=-10x-\\frac{k{x}^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nNow, since $v=12\\,m/s$ when $x=0\\,m,$ we can find the value of the constant $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =-10x-\\frac{k{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(12)^{2} & =-10(0)-\\frac{k(0)^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ C & =72\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}=72-10x-\\frac{k{x}^{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $v=2\\sqrt{15}\\,m/s$ when $x=4\\,m,$ we can find the value of the positive constant $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =72-10x-\\frac{k{x}^{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(2\\sqrt{15})^{2} & =72-10(4)-\\frac{k(4)^{2}}{2} \\\\ 30 & =72-40-8k \\\\ 8k & =2 \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365336 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365337 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365336 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365338 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365336 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365339 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365336 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365340 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365336 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365341 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365336 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365336 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365336 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365340 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365336 1080 #uuid "9f1e0c06-6d19-53