4139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365386 1081 "(-6,3)" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365386 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365386 1084 #uuid "f36a60a4-00a7-5e6a-85cb-be21c1d6c7c3" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365387 1081 "(2,5)" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365387 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365387 1084 #uuid "57fb3340-e9e8-5743-ad50-c056aedb52fc" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365388 1081 "(6,-3)" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365388 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365388 1084 #uuid "0761c73f-5cba-5258-8c22-9d3fc9a8d8d0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365389 1081 "(3,6)" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365389 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365389 1084 #uuid "ed2cd59f-1f8d-5835-bdd1-f2019ae4d1c6" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365390 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365391 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365390 1069 "q-164127" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365390 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365390 1071 "Let $R=[0,1]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=3x-4y+6.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365390 1072 #uuid "a486be22-0dc3-5ead-b006-67b72d5b0fef" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365390 1074 "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=3x-4y+6$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=3x-4y+6$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/a4/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=3{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j}+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(3{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j}+6)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $3{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j}+6.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365391 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365392 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365391 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365393 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365391 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365394 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365391 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365395 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365391 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365396 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365391 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365391 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true]