 1072 #uuid "059a7498-ddb3-55e8-bcb5-59a377de1ec3" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365459 1074 "We start by calculating the derivative of $f$ at the point $(0,1).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{3}+{e}^{x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2}+{e}^{x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(0,1)$ lies on $y=f(x),$ we know that the corresponding point $(1,0)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nFurthermore, the slopes of the tangents to the two respective points are reciprocals. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(1))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365461 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365462 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365463 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365464 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365465 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365460 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365460 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365460 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365464 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365460 1080 #uuid "e5fbd0d0-3471-59b4-9681-197e01286a0b" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365461 1081 "\\frac{2e}{3}" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365461 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365461 1084 #uuid "b743c013-d7e2-57ee-b495-0b7f0dde5cbd" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365462 1081 "3" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365462 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365462 1084 #uuid "c639d361-236a-5d9b-a0f1-b0090d6c2520" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365463 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533447 17592186045