ted at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be re-written as\n\n$$\n{J}_{f}({x}_{n})({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-f({x}_{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the Jacobian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{J}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}-4{y}^{3}-1) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}-4{y}^{3}-1) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}-2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2} & -12{y}^{2} \\\\ 2x & 8y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2} & -12{y}^{2} \\\\ 2x & 8y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-{[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-4{y}^{3}-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2} & -12{y}^{2} \\\\ 2x & 8y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-4{y}^{3}-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3(1)^{2} & -12(1)^{2} \\\\ 2(1) & 8(1)\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-[\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}-4(1)^{3}-1 \\\\ (1)^{2}+4(1)^{2}-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & -12 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365467 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365468 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365467 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365467 1077 "field-1" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365467 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365468 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365467 1080 #uuid "0844a9f9-3325-5e66-a8c3-cc1717c4a969" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365468 1081 "-12" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365468 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365468 1084 #uuid "0f3a8d0f-aa86-5d63-8c72-1351742792