 integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}f({x}_{m})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{m}=a+mΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{8}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x+1)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x+1),$ the lower bound is $a=2$ and the upper bound is $b=8.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{8-2}{n}=\\frac{6}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{8}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}f({x}_{m})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[f(2+m\\cdot \\frac{6}{n})\\cdot \\frac{6}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[f(2+\\frac{6m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{6}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5(2+\\frac{6m}{n})+1)\\cdot \\frac{6}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(11+\\frac{30m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{6}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365578 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365579 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365578 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365578 1077 "field-1" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365578 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365579 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365578 1080 #uuid "07649995-d867-534f-9e43-6b83134b223f" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365579 1081 "11+\\frac{30m}{n}" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365579 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365579 1084 #uuid "0bce27b2-5df3-5a8e-869e-d080b7d5082b" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365580 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365581 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365580 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365583 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365580 1069 "q-326016" 13194139533447 17592186045585 