1069 "q-33627" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365730 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365730 1071 "Which of the following gives the unit tangent vector to the curve\n $r(t)=⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,t,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (0,\\infty )?$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365730 1072 #uuid "999eae56-9014-5e14-ac70-9c3dd9daada7" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365730 1074 "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),\\,y(t),\\,z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\sqrt{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,1,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})}^{2}+(1)^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}+1+\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1+{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}}{{t}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{(1+{t}^{2})^{2}}{{t}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{t}^{2}}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Finally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1+{t}^{2}}⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,1,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{t}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}⟨-1,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365731 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365732 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365731 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365733 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365731 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365734 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365731 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365735 1319413953344