\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}3t{e}^{t} \\\\ t{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int 3t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int t{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating the components by parts, we get the following:\n\n- For the first component, let $u=3t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=3\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v={e}^{t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(3t)\\cdot {e}^{t}-\\int {e}^{t}\\cdot (3\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =3t{e}^{t}-3{e}^{t} \\\\  & =3{e}^{t}(t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, let $u=t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=1\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int t{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(t)\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{2})\\cdot (1\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{t{e}^{-2t}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{4}(2t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & 2{e}^{2t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-t} & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{t}(t-1) \\\\ -\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{4}(2t+1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}12(t-1)-2(2t+1) \\\\ 24(t-1)-(2t+1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}8t-14 \\\\ 22t-25\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365807 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365808 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365807 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365807 1077 "field-1" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365807 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365808 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365807 1080 #uuid "108a4f0f-4662-57f5-8305-95c9666f98fc" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365808 1081 "22t-25" 13194139533447 17592186045585 