\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\lambda x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\lambda x).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-6A\\lambda \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\lambda x)+6B\\lambda \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\lambda x).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ yields\n\n$$\n-6A\\lambda \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+6B\\lambda \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=0\n$$\n\nwhich gives $B=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\lambda x).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition $y(3)=0$ yields\n\n$$\nA\\operatorname{cos}⁡(18\\lambda )=0.\n$$\n\nFor nontrivial solutions, we require \n\n$$\n18\\lambda =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi =\\frac{(2n+1)\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\nfor $n\\in N.$ This gives the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{n}=\\frac{(2n+1)\\pi }{36}.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding eigenfunctions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{n}(x)={B}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6{\\lambda }_{n}x),\\,{B}_{n}\\in R.\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365876 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365877 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365876 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365878 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365876 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365879 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365876 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365880 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365876 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365881 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365876 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365876 1077 "field-1" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365876 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365881 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365876 1080 #uuid "90babee2-f98c-50aa-ba37-d79ed5ae8e0b" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365877 1081 "\\frac{n\\pi }{18}" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365877 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365877 1084 #uuid "6b9eadc9-cd9b-51ab-ade7-9f484b76759c" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365878 1081 "\\frac{n\\pi }{36}" 1319413953