\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365960 1072 #uuid "fdb89387-1831-5dc9-8b54-30b782e40107" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365960 1074 "Recall that the general solution of a linear differential equation of the form ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(x)$ is given by $y={y}_{c}+{y}_{p},$ where ${y}_{c}$ is the solution to the homogeneous equation and ${y}_{p}$ is a particular solution.\n\nFirst, we address the particular solution ${y}_{p}.$ Since $f(x)$ is an even function and the differential operator contains no ${y}^{′}$ (damping) term, the particular solution inherits the symmetry and is also an even function consisting only of cosine terms. This is represented by the term\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nNext, we find the homogeneous solution. The characteristic equation ${\\lambda }^{2}+8=0$ gives roots $\\lambda =\\pm \\sqrt{8}\\text{i}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{8}x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{8}x).\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we apply the initial conditions. Differentiating the total solution gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)∼-A\\sqrt{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{8}x)+B\\sqrt{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{8}x)-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(0) & =-A\\sqrt{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+B\\sqrt{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\ 0 & =0+B\\sqrt{8}-0 \\\\ B & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because the total solution is an even function, its derivative is an odd function, which must vanish at $x=0.$\n\nNext, we use the condition $y(0)=-2.$ With $B=0,$ the total solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)∼A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{8}x)+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nApplying $y(0)=-2$ and noting that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =A+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n} \\\\ A & =-2-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A$ back into ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{8}x),$ we find the missing part:\n\n$$\ny(x)∼\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{8}x)(-2-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n})+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365961 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365962 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365961 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365963 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365961 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365964 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365961 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365965 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365961 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365961 1077 "field-1" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365961 1079 #edb/ref 17592186365962 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365961 1080 #uuid "9ab9d6fd-f448-55e9-b96d-b8b72364ed81" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365962 1081 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{8}x)(-2-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n})" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365962 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365962 1084 #uuid "c43daebb-d90e-5f56-8f36-6c2339f67f42" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365963 1081 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{8}x)({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+2)" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365963 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365963 1084 #uuid "abb08875-6849-5046-819a-ba8c196e97ed" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365964 1081 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{8}x)(-2+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n})" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365964 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186365964 1084 #uuid "3639c708-e27d-5c89-b671-db99d9bc675a" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [175921