7592186045585 true] [17592186366124 1072 #uuid "dbf56628-94da-5878-ab0e-12187baa0d83" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366124 1074 "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{3\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 0+4\\cdot 2}{{4}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize each vector to get an orthonormal basis.\n\n- ${u}_{1}=\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- ${u}_{2}=\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthonormal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=-\\frac{1}{3},$ $b=\\frac{2}{3},$ $c=\\frac{2}{3}$ and  \n\n$$\n|a|+|b|+|c|=|-\\frac{1}{3}|+|\\frac{2}{3}|+|\\frac{2}{3}|=\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$" 13194139533447 