bda -1)-3\\lambda +5] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-3\\lambda +5 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +5 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve the auxiliary equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +5 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4)-4+5 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda -2 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =2\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =2\\pm \\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2+\\text{i}} & ={x}^{2}{e}^{\\text{i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}={x}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)), \\\\ {x}^{2-\\text{i}} & ={x}^{2}{e}^{-\\text{i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}={x}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =A{x}^{2+\\text{i}}+B{x}^{2-\\text{i}} \\\\  & =A{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))+B{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & =(A+B){x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}(A-B){x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite $y(x)$ as\n\n$$\ny(x)={x}^{2}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366178 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366179 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366178 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366180 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366178 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366181 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366178 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366182 13194139533447 1759218604