egin{aligned}r & =c+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\ r & =⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,1,1⟩+t⟨-4,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366212 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366213 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366212 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366214 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366212 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366215 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366212 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366216 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366212 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366217 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366212 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366212 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366212 1079 #edb/ref 17592186366217 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366212 1080 #uuid "3b9dde6c-05bb-5b0d-9060-015e400fc047" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366213 1081 "r=⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,1,1⟩+t⟨-3,2,4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366213 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366213 1084 #uuid "abe04ef1-0077-539a-b85c-52caa98344a5" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366214 1081 "The plane is undefined" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366214 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366214 1084 #uuid "4a96f288-3fd0-537b-806e-046844764150" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366215 1081 "r=⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨-3,2,4⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366215 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366215 1084 #uuid "fac45cd4-59c7-516c-bd74-1e4a54e263c2" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366216 1081 "r=⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,1,1⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366216 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366216 1084 #uuid "4e15b755-6aa5-59e8-8ede-166d794590c7" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366217 1081 "r=⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,1,1⟩+t⟨-4,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366217 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366217 1084 #uuid "6d4ca503-3a78-5aa5-ac98-b7e77b80a651" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366218 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366219 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366218 1069 "q-71415" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366218 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366218 1071 "The intersection of the planes $3x+6y+3z=0$ and $x-y+2z+3=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},{a}_{2},0⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366218 1072 #uuid "56b3e332-cb62-524a-a627-2ac9bac6fdaa" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366218 1074 "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $z=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation gives  \n\n$$\n3x+6y+3(0)=0\\,⟹\\,x=-2y,\n$$\n\nand substituting $z=0$ and $x=-2y$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z+3 & =0 \\\\ -2y-y+2(0)+3 & =0 \\\\ -3y & =-3 \\\\ y & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=-2y=-2$ and $a=⟨-2,1,0⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $3x+6y+3z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,6,3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-y+2z+3=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,2⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,6,3⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =15i-3j-9k \\\\  & =⟨15,-3,-9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can pick any vector that is parallel to ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}$ as a direction vector of the line. So, let \n\n$$\nb=\\frac{1}{3}({n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2})=⟨5,-1,-3⟩.\n$$\n\nThe equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨-2,1,0⟩+t⟨5,-1,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-2+1=-1,$ and $b=⟨5,-1,-3⟩.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366219 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366220 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366219 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366221 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366219 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366222 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366219 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366223 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366219 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366224 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366219 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366219 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366219 1079 #edb/ref 17592186366224 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366219 1080 #uuid "fe204930-21f0-5f11-87d8-144b4ea013e0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366220 1081 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-2,\\,b=⟨5,-1,3⟩" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366220 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366220 1084 #uuid "3221a9ad-33cd-5589-8d04-58da9238940e" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366221 1081 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=0,\\,b=⟨3,-1,-5⟩" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366221 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366221 1084 #uuid "c700d7ec-2dc4-5c91-b31f-02251699ee00" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366222 1081 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=2,\\,b=⟨5,1,3⟩" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366222 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366222 1084 #uuid "50edec43-8dae-5c9f-ab3b-07f67a03c9d5" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366223 1081 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=1,\\,b=⟨5,1,-3⟩" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366223 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366223 1084 #uuid "0fe78330-aad4-5b51-9fc7-f31f9d446de9" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366224 1081 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-1,\\,b=⟨5,-1,-3⟩" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366224 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366224 1084 #uuid "86b7c672-b3df-5dbe-8e30-f48eb2411bdb" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366225 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366226 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366225 1069 "q-71448" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366225 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366225 1071 "Given the two planes $x-2y+z=0$ and $x-y+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n- The planes intersect on a line." 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366225 1072 #uuid "96c9a429-d310-55eb-845b-95fc86ca78d5" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366225 1074 "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-2y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-2,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-2,1⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366226 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366227 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366226 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366228 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366226 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366229 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366226 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366230 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366226 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366231 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366226 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366226 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366226 1079 #edb/ref 17592186366229 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366226 1080 #uuid "8a7171c3-579f-5a05-8896-bebb6c2c2177" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366227 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366227 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366227 1084 #uuid "ab715e39-7262-53f8-a589-7932e5948409" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366228 1081 "I only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366228 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366228 1084 #uuid "4df91f2a-726d-5a75-89e2-fbf683b5f3e6" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366229 1081 "III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366229 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366229 1084 #uuid "15089811-be63-5322-bff3-9d9751b255f4" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366230 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366230 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366230 1084 #uuid "73dbba28-230f-587a-b4f0-389b59e14572" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366231 1081 "II only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366231 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366231 1084 #uuid "d97b5ca9-cd86-5251-bc55-f166bb43da71" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366232 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366233 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366232 1069 "q-7202" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366232 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366232 1071 "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=(2t+1)^{3}$, where $t>0$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=\\frac{65}{8}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=1\\,\\text{s}$, determine the moment in time when the particle is stationary." 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366232 1072 #uuid "b219724a-8fbc-5643-88ad-38f4f5993b95" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366232 1074 "The particle is stationary when $v=0\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$\n\nFirst, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (2t+1)^{3}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(2t+1)^{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=\\frac{65}{8}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{65}{8} & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot {[2(1)+1]}^{4}+C \\\\ \\frac{65}{8} & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot (81)+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{65}{8}-\\frac{81}{8} \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{1}{8}(2t+1)^{4}-2.$\n\nNow, we find the moments in time when $v=0\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}(2t+1)^{4}-2 & =0 \\\\ (2t+1)^{4} & =16 \\\\ 2t+1 & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $t=-\\frac{3}{2}\\,,\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nSince $t>0$, we discard solution $t=-\\frac{3}{2}.$ \nTherefore, the particle is stationary when $t=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{s}.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366233 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366234 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366233 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366235 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366233 1075 #edb/re