.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366273 1072 #uuid "101958a5-0fd4-5f49-ac03-dbd002fe3b2a" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366273 1074 "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=7-2x-3y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=7-2x-3y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/4a/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=7-2{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(7-2{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $7-2{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j}.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366274 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366275 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366274 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366276 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366274 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366277 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366274 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366278 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366274 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366279 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366274 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366274 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366274 1079 #edb/ref 17592186366279 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366274 1080 #uuid "a52cab97-c8fe-5f62-8cf4-6a0a2d6a633d" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366275 1081 "7-2{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j-1}" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366275 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366275 1084 #uuid "088a5a27-7121-5ef2-975b-f0cb92043a6b" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366276 1081 "7-2{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366276 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366276 1084 #uuid "446a494d-7af6-549e-a8bc-5cb2e079ae36" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366277 1081 "{x}_{i}+3{y}_{j}" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366277 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366277 1084 #uuid "413575d7-38da-50e8-98b3-0ba725b54022" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366278 1081 "{x}_{i-1}+3{y}_{j-1}" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366278 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366278 1084 #uuid "b2a5f0df-7922-5df9-a55a-829b8e9ae3b3" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366279 1081 "7-2{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j}" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366279 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366279 1084 #uuid "9a856b90-6780-5bd7-8d0a-d3cc30b049a4" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366280 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366281 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366280 1069 "q-76108" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366280 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366280 1071 "Consider the function $f(x)={2}^{x}+1.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(5).$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366280 1072 #uuid "67a843ac-f40c-59da-8377-455b0890a108" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366280 1074 "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(5),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(5)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(5))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(5).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(5)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(5) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =5 \\\\ {2}^{x}+1 & =5 \\\\ {2}^{x} & =4 \\\\ {2}^{x} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{-1}(5)=2.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={2}^{x}+1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot {2}^{x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(5) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(5))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366281 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366282 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366281 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366283 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366281 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366284 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366281 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366285 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366281 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366286 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366281 1076