3194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366635 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366636 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366635 1069 "q-95397" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366635 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366635 1071 "Consider the change of variables given by the matrix equation\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand the curve $C,$ defined as\n\n$$\nC:\\,{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+4\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1}=4.\n$$\n\n \n\nGiven that the change of variables above reduces $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ to its canonical (diagonal) form $2{y}_{1}^{2}$ what type of a quadratic curve is defined by $C?$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366635 1072 #uuid "3c25a282-f09e-5080-ae4d-6a92631e6519" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366635 1074 "First, we note the following:\n\n$$\nC:\\,{{{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}+4\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1}=4\n$$\n\nLet's write the given change of variables explicitly:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{1}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{1}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the given change of variables reduces $Q(x)$ to its canonical form. Therefore, performing the change of variables on $C,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+4\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1} & =4 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}^{2}+4\\sqrt{2}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{1}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2}) & =4 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{1}-4{y}_{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we complete the square for the variable ${y}_{1}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{1}-4{y}_{2} & =4 \\\\ 2({y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{1})-4{y}_{2} & =4 \\\\ 2({y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{1}+1-1)-4{y}_{2} & =4 \\\\ 2({y}_{1}+1)^{2}-2\\cdot 1-4{y}_{2} & =4 \\\\ 2({y}_{1}+1)^{2} & =4{y}_{2}+6 \\\\ 2({y}_{1}+1)^{2} & =4({y}_{2}+\\frac{3}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, performing the change of variables \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{z}_{1}={y}_{1}+1, \\\\ {z}_{2}={y}_{2}+\\frac{3}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({y}_{1}+1)^{2} & =4({y}_{2}+\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\ 2{z}_{1}^{2} & =4{z}_{2} \\\\ {z}_{1}^{2} & =2{z}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis represents a parabola that opens in the direction of the positive ${z}_{2}$-axis." 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366636 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366637 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366636 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366638 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366636 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366639 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366636 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366640 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366636 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366641 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366636 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366636 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366636 1079 #edb/ref 17592186366639 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366636 1080 #uuid "23070fd2-4a47-5c26-ae55-52058929b2df" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366637 1081 "A pair of intersecting lines" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366637 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366637 1084 #uuid "b13d7123-12c3-5fba-865d-79d04d134405" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366638 1081 "An empty set" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366638 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366638 1084 #uuid "9eb75fec-aad0-52b8-8f0b-256603947924" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366639 1081 "A parabola" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366639 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366639 1084 #uuid "335c53ad-9b06-5ae9-9d82-ab45fdedd159" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366640 1081 "A pair of parallel lines" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366640 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366640 1084 #uuid "50865aa7-b849-5510-a201-43adab487ed6" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366641 1081 "A hyperbola with semiaxes  $3$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366641 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366641 1084 #uuid "30cf17d6-9da7-5a11-b299-70e72069e0e0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366642 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366643 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366642 1069 "q-95405" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366642 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366642 1071 "Given that $A$ is an $8\\times 8$ real symmetric matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable\n- $A$ must have $8$ real and distinct eigenvalues\n- If $u$ and $v$ are two eigenvectors that correspond to different eigenvalues, then $u⊥v$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366642 1072 #uuid "66a9cbb1-7460-5af7-96d5-cd936a2ef154" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366642 1074 "Given that $A$ is an $n\\times n$ symmetric matrix over $R$, the spectral theorem states the following:\n\n- The eigenvalues of $A$ are all real.\n\n- Eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues are orthogonal.\n\n- The dimension of the eigenspace for each eigenvalue equals the multiplicity of that eigenvalue as a root of the characteristic polynomial.\n\n- $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, any symmetric matrix with real entries is orthogonally diagonalizable.\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the spectral theorem, the eigenvalues are real but not necessarily distinct. This occurs when the characteristic polynomial has roots whose (algebraic) multiplicity is greater than $1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues must be orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366643 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366644 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366643 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366645 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366643 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366646 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366643 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366647 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366643 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366648 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366643 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366643 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366643 1079 #edb/ref 17592186366644 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366643 1080 #uuid "0c5dfe21-2503-5ca5-ba06-5e40538f2c86" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366644 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366644 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366644 1084 #uuid "f6c043df-b951-508f-a8ac-a622bdff16b7" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366645 1081 "I only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366645 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366645 1084 #uuid "952832fc-ad00-5ff2-84c8-e9a9c82cbf2e" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366646 1081 "III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366646 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366646 1084 #uuid "4feb2e46-4dfb-5f30-8616-25de093d73a0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366647 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366647 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366647 1084 #uuid "1403c16c-f9d1-5cf9-9e2b-5c88279db56e" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366648 1081 "II only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366648 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366648 1084 #uuid "7d670dd8-c6f5-5af7-880e-caccf78560d0" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366649 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366650 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366649 1069 "q-95409" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366649 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366649 1071 "Given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ real symmetric matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is not diagonalizable\n- If $u$ and $v$ are two eigenvectors that correspond to different eigenvalues, then $u⊥v$\n- $A$ must have $4$ real (not necessarily distinct) eigenvalues" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366649 1072 #uuid "42059a97-8b39-59cb-bae6-eab5799ef586" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366649 1074 "Given that $A$ is an $n\\times n$ symmetric matrix over $R$, the spectral theorem states the following:\n\n- The eigenvalues of $A$ are all real.\n\n- Eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues are orthogonal.\n\n- The dimension of the eigenspace for each eigenvalue equals the multiplicity of that eigenvalue as a root of the characteristic polynomial.\n\n- $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the theorem, any symmetric matrix with real entries is orthogonally diagonalizable, hence, is diagonalizable.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues must be orthogonal.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, a $4\\times 4$ matrix has $4$ (not necessarily distinct) eigenvalues and the eigenvalues of a symmetric matrix are real.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366650 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366651 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366650 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366652 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366650 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366653 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366650 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366654 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366650 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366655 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366650 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366650 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366650 1079 #edb/ref 17592186366652 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366650 1080 #uuid "6d83eaf8-43d8-5306-a69f-c49ea4983f73" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366651 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366651 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366651 1084 #uuid "02712a35-380c-5af0-8612-4958a1f8625b" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366652 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366652 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366652 1084 #uuid "08bdc7f8-45b5-5d17-9e52-976b4685ca5e" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366653 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366653 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366653 1084 #uuid "a302555e-ddb4-54c9-8f7c-597f415e28de" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366654 1081 "III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366654 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366654 1084 #uuid "f7f68b13-086a-524d-87f0-06