66722 1084 #uuid "2bcd63bc-bb9a-572f-82b4-47762607136e" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366723 1081 "{C}_{4}\\,:\\,{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2}=1" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366723 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366723 1084 #uuid "c5e5413f-cae3-5a1a-b51c-0f5d02afb311" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366724 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366725 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366724 1069 "q-95897" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366724 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366724 1071 "Which of the following equations define a non-empty set of points in the ${x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ plane?\n\n- $2{x}_{2}^{2}+1=0$\n- $-2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}=2$\n- ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}=0$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366724 1072 #uuid "66610d66-38e7-5d9e-b883-9467a5f6ad73" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366724 1074 "Let's examine each of the equations in turn.\n\n- The equation $2{x}_{2}^{2}+1=0$ defines an empty set. Notice that the left-hand side is positive for all ${x}_{2},$ while the right-hand side is zero.\n\n- The equation $-2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}=2$ defines an empty set. Notice that the left-hand side is non-positive for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ while the right-hand side is  positive.\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}=0$ defines a non-empty set in the ${x}_{1}{x}_{2}$-plane. It represents a parabola that opens in the direction of the negative ${x}_{2}$-axis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366725 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366726 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366725 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366727 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366725 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366728 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366725 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366729 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366725 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366730 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366725 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366725 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366725 1079 #edb/ref 17592186366728 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366725 1080 #uuid "9b490a57-fb54-5a0a-88db-c6476bcf4020" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366726 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366726 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366726 1084 #uuid "74284b82-6c00-50fb-87d1-3ddbcaf76ea7" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366727 1081 "I only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366727 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366727 1084 #uuid "e6f287e6-fc5a-5612-b6dc-6230a07c50e7" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366728 1081 "III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366728 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366728 1084 #uuid "c06a6c66-9a0d-5f1b-9652-7f1a9fa3de3b" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366729 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366729 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366729 1084 #uuid "104fff1c-e7d5-577f-9a3f-09e2515d3988" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366730 1081 "II only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366730 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366730 1084 #uuid "8de9089d-d7bc-5109-9499-41d65a155982" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366731 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366732 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366731 1069 "q-96067" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366731 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366731 1071 "What type of quadratic curve is defined by the following equation?\n\n$$\n3{x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=9\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366731 1072 #uuid "7d74d7da-0e93-513c-8a0b-cbe7ece164cb" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366731 1074 "First, we complete the squares for the variables ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2} & =9 \\\\ 3({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1})-({x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{2}) & =9 \\\\ 3({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}+1-1)-({x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{2}+9-9) & =9 \\\\ 3({x}_{1}-1)^{2}-3-({x}_{2}-3)^{2}+9 & =9 \\\\ 3({x}_{1}-1)^{2}-({x}_{2}-3)^{2} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, performing the change of variables\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-1, \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}-3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({x}_{1}-1)^{2}-({x}_{2}-3)^{2} & =3 \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{{\\sqrt{3}}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis represents a hyperbola with semiaxes $1$ and $\\sqrt{3}.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366733 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366734 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366735 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366736 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366737 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366732 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366732 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366732 1079 #edb/ref 17592186366736 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366732 1080 #uuid "66665b04-8cc0-542f-ad9b-e8d5d6255ced" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366733 1081 "A single point" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366733 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366733 1084 #uuid "9905cbf0-c114-5744-928d-549e3bb50896" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366734 1081 "An ellipse with semiaxes $\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366734 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366734 1084 #uuid "9e16170d-702e-59ac-b59e-0c7868a93b97" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366735 1081 "A pair of intersecting lines" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366735 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366735 1084 #uuid "80dbb7a6-0d32-5adc-8510-5b0aaf2c2838" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366736 1081 "A hyperbola with semiaxes $1$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366736 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366736 1084 #uuid "8f72c2ee-efca-59b0-87ff-0f833655ad91" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366737 1081 "A parabola" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366737 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366737 1084 #uuid "7a752195-1acf-532a-b58a-41a03894c235" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366738 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366739 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366738 1069 "q-96075" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366738 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366738 1071 "What type of quadratic curve is defined by the following equation?\n\n$$\n3{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}^{2}=\\frac{35}{3}\n$$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366738 1072 #uuid "bb83c793-f479-5cb9-b03e-05eb6c2cfac2" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366738 1074 "First, we complete the squares for the variable ${x}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}^{2} & =\\frac{35}{3} \\\\ 3({x}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{1})+4{x}_{2}^{2} & =\\frac{35}{3} \\\\ 3({x}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{1}+{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2})+4{x}_{2}^{2} & =\\frac{35}{3} \\\\ 3{({x}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-3{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2} & =\\frac{35}{3} \\\\ 3{({x}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}+4{x}_{2}^{2} & =\\frac{35}{3} \\\\ 3{({x}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2} & =\\frac{36}{3} \\\\ 3{({x}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, performing the change of variables\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3}, \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{2}^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis represents an ellipse with semiaxes $2$ and $\\sqrt{3}.$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366739 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366740 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366739 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366741 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366739 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366742 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366739 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366743 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366739 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366744 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366739 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366739 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366739 1079 #edb/ref 17592186366744 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366739 1080 #uuid "296453d6-3c71-5737-82c3-c5c36630c17c" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366740 1081 "A single point" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366740 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366740 1084 #uuid "050d3072-c838-5e08-b0bc-4d5171d8a819" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366741 1081 "A hyperbola with semiaxes $\\sqrt{2}$ and $3$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366741 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366741 1084 #uuid "e5183501-b9cd-5561-b6e3-c0b1b0bb5462" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366742 1081 "A parabola" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366742 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366742 1084 #uuid "c04e7a5e-a95d-5547-bc90-7be6e5c15598" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366743 1081 "A pair of parallel lines" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366743 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366743 1084 #uuid "3ed40f62-9010-5b5c-bf46-6927e9dc6923" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366744 1081 "An ellipse with semiaxes $2$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366744 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366744 1084 #uuid "4d718142-0fc1-5c0e-bd69-6c41ab31ffc5" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366745 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366746 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366745 1069 "q-96594" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366745 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366745 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The sum of two $n\\times n$ diagonal matrices is always symmetric.\n- If $A$ is *any* $n\\times n$ matrix, then ${A}^{-1}$ is always symmetric (if it exists).\n- If $A$ is *any* matrix, then ${A}^{T}A$ is always symmetric." 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366745 1072 #uuid "df6e5142-313f-5de3-a45d-4da4b737f0bd" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366745 1074 "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any diagonal matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}+{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, consider the non-singular matrix \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nHowever, ${A}^{-1}$ is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({A}^{T}A)^{T} & ={A}^{T}({A}^{T})^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366746 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366747 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366746 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366748 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366746 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366749 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366746 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366750 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366746 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366751 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366746 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366746 1077 "selection" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366746 1079 #edb/ref 17592186366748 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366746 1080 #uuid "df5f5020-3bfe-5ba9-ac48-5edeee6702ce" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366747 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366747 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366747 1084 #uuid "87f9de83-c305-5216-bce3-dd9349ecfed7" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366748 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366748 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366748 1084 #uuid "eaf94fab-b385-52a0-af41-6d00f4a5dbd7" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366749 1081 "I only" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366749 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [17592186366749 1084 #uuid "fb5e63ab-43e7-5367-a64a-8da7db506d01" 13194139533447 17592186045585 true] [1759